SUMMARY:Local Art Live!
DESCRIPTION:Thursday May 14th\, 2026\nDoors | 6:00 PM\nShow | 6:30 PM \nEvent Ticket | $19.30 + Fees \nThis event is all ages – 21+ With Valid ID Required to Drink\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\n—————————————————\nPresented by Mickey’s Black Box\n—————————————————\nCome out and enjoy a great night of live music\, artistic expression\, and delicious drinks – highlighting the incredible talent in our backyard! \nFeaturing Local Artists – Johnny Zarfati\, Dylan Zangwill\, Barkley Cove\, & Easy Brother \nJohnny Zarfati\nJohnny Zarfati is a New Jersey based Americana artist. He draws on the grit of the northeast and the soul of American roots music to craft a sound that feels both “lived in” and fresh. Blending Folk\, Americana\, and alt country his music searches for something real. Part Troubadour\, part poet\, grounded in tradition but unafraid to carve his own path.\nWebsite | Instagram \nDylan Zangwill\nIn 2022\, Dylan traveled to Nashville where he worked with Grammy Award-Winning producer John Carter Cash at the legendary Cash Cabin\, recording 4 of Dylan’s original songs. Late in 2022\, Dylan appeared on American Idol Season 21 where he amazed the judges with an original composition\, “Bittersweet Melody” and received his Golden Ticket to Hollywood.  Following Idol\, he went back to the studio to record more originals\, this time with producer Adam Weiner and the backing of Adam’s band\, Low Cut Connie. He’s performed at venues of all sizes throughout the Philadelphia metro area and has also taken the show on the road to Delaware\, Maryland\, Nashville\, New Orleans\, Los Angeles\, Hollywood\, Austin\, Florida\, New York\, and even London audiences. Dylan’s signature sound is unmistakable: powerful vocals\, refined piano and guitar playing\, and enthralling originals\, delivered with a unique and engaging blend of bluesy rock and Southwestern flair.\nWebsite | Instagram | Facebook \nBarkley Cove\nBarkley Cove is the band to watch in the new folk scene. Raised on collaborative songwriting\, rich vocal harmony\, and the folk revival records of the 60s and beyond\, members Jillian Dolan (guitar)\, Yusuf Miller (mandolin)\, Silas Gross (banjo)\, and Robert Myers (bass) mix genres of folk\, rock\, country\, and bluegrass to create a distinctly original sound that will linger in your ear long after the last chord. As their reach expands throughout the United States\, Barkley Cove’s imaginative songwriting and dedication to originality continue to push the boundaries of new folk music.\nWebsite | Instagram | Facebook \nEasy Brother\nFeaturing Dan Merger – Vocals / Clifton Conrad – Guitar / Mike Santarelli – Guitar / Ryan Campbell – Bass / Mark Kerper – Keys / Adam Moyer – Drums\nFacebook \nFeaturing Local Vendors: Fractured Frog\, Kate Rush Art\, Northern Liberties Design\, Jenni Buffington Art\, & Breezy Soaps Co\n—————————————————\n*Ticket Alert*  \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers.  Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets.  Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/local-art-live/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://mickeysblackbox.com/app/uploads/2026/02/LOCAL-ART-LIVE-NEW-1-e1775944609394.png
END:VEVENT
