SUMMARY:An Evening of Comedy to Benefit Warwick Community Ambulance Association
DESCRIPTION:Saturday May 16th\, 2026\nDoors | 7:00 PM\nShow | 8:00 PM \nReserved Mezzanine Seating | $34.70 + Fees\nReserved Riser Seating | $40.20 + Fees\nReserved Balcony Seating | $40.20 + Fees\nReserved Table Seating | $45.30 + Fees \n+$5 on All Day of Show Purchases\nPlease note\, this event is 18+ – 21+ With Valid ID to Drink\nPlease note\, this show contains adult content.\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\n—————————————————\nPresented by Franco’s Comedy For Your Cause\n—————————————————\nFeaturing Tracy Locke\, Avery Quinn\, & Sean Morton!  \nSince 1956\, Warwick Community Ambulance has proudly served Lititz and the surrounding communities with 24/7 emergency medical care. Every dollar raised through this comedy night stays right here at home\, supporting local ambulances\, equipment\, training\, and the providers who respond when our neighbors need help. By buying a ticket\, you are directly investing in the care of your community and helping ensure Warwick EMS is ready when it matters most. \nTracy Locke\nTake the all American girl next door\, add a pinch of devilish charm\, a dash of sports fanatic\, some raw charisma\, sprinkle in kooky\, eclectic characters set on high speed and POW! the perfect recipe for comedy. Tracy Locke has been performing as a professional comedian for over 18 years\, from sold out shows at Radio City Music Hall to comedy clubs across the nation. She has hosted television\, live events and award shows as well as co-founding the corporate training company Productively Funny which specializes in custom-made\, interactive corporate training workshops. \nAvery Quinn\nAvery Quinn is a comedian originally from Lititz\, PA\, now residing in Hartford\, CT. He was the winner of the 2024 Last Comix Standing contest at Comix Roadhouse at Mohegan Sun Casino. Avery has been making audiences laugh since 2018 with his physical comedy and absurd observations all across the East Coast.  He has headlined at Comix Roadhouse at Mohegan Sun\, the BrewHaha in Wethersfield CT\, City Winery in New York and Western New England University.  Avery has featured at various comedy clubs and colleges including New York Comedy Club Stamford\, Stress Factory in Bridgeport CT\, Dojo of Comedy in New Jersey\, and UCONN.  He was also a featured performer at the Portland Maine Comedy Festival and a semifinalist in the 2020 Philly’s Phunniest Comic contest at Helium Comedy Club.  Avery has made appearances on Investigation Discovery and Oxygen Network. \nSean Morton\nA veteran road comic for over 17 years\, Sean has performed at clubs and casinos across the US\, was a member of the legendary Friars Club\, and released his first stand-up special in 2024\, which landed in the top 10 of the comedy charts.\n—————————————————\n*Ticket Alert*  \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers.  Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets.  Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/an-evening-of-comedy-to-benefit-warwick-community-ambulance-association/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
